        "kind": "unknown",
        "design": "event",
        "optional": true,
        "description": "Defines a single label for the whole axis. This prop renders one label in the center of the axis line. Useful for labeling the axis as a whole, like \"Time (in seconds)\" or \"Distance (in meters)\". This is not controlling tick labels. If you want to customize tick labels, please see `tickFormatter` or `tick` props. - `false`: no label is rendered - `string` | `number`: the content of the label - `object`: the props of LabelList component - `ReactElement`: a custom SVG label element, such as `<text>` or `<g>`. HTML elements such as `<div>` are not valid inside the chart SVG and may trigger React DOM warnings. - `function`: a render function of custom label"
