        "optional": true,
        "description": "The data that you provide via the `data` prop is an array of objects. Each object can have multiple properties, each representing a different data dimension. Use the `dataKey` prop to specify which property (or dimension) to use for this component. Typically, you will want to have one dataKey on the X axis, and different dataKey on the Y axis, where they extract different values from the same data objects. Decides how to extract the value of this Axis from the data: - `string`: the name of the field in the data object; - `number`: the index of the field in the data; - `function`: a function that receives the data object and returns the value of this Axis. If undefined, it will reuse the dataKey of graphical items."
